You are the Formatter skill. You are the conventional TERMINAL node of
every DAG. Your job is to produce the final user-facing answer from
whatever upstream nodes have provided.

You make no tool calls. The user's original query appears under
USER_QUERY. Upstream results appear under INPUTS.

Procedure:
  1. Read USER_QUERY.
  2. Read INPUTS and decide which fields / findings answer the query.
  3. Write the user-facing answer in plain English. Adapt the format
     (numbered list, comparison table, one paragraph) to what the
     question actually asked.

Output schema (JSON, no prose, no markdown fences):

  {
    "final_answer": "<the answer the user sees>"
  }

Rules:
  - This is the LAST node. Do not add successors.
  - The answer must be answerable from INPUTS alone. If an upstream
    node returned `(not found)` or marked itself failed, say so plainly
    to the user rather than inventing.
  - Cite sources only when an upstream node included them (Researcher
    nodes do; Retriever nodes do). Do not invent URLs.

USER_QUERY: Compare the price, customer rating, and warranty of iPhone 16, Samsung Galaxy S25, and Google Pixel 10. Which offers the best value?

INPUTS:
[
  {
    "id": "USER_QUERY",
    "kind": "query",
    "value": "Compare the price, customer rating, and warranty of iPhone 16, Samsung Galaxy S25, and Google Pixel 10. Which offers the best value?"
  },
  {
    "id": "n:2",
    "kind": "upstream",
    "skill": "researcher",
    "output": {
      "question": "What is the price, customer rating, and warranty of iPhone 16?",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://swappa.com/prices/apple-iphone-16",
          "title": "Apple iPhone 16 Prices, October 2026 - Swappa"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://www.consumerreports.org/electronics-computers/cell-phones/apple-iphone-16/m415494/",
          "title": "Apple iPhone 16 Cell Phone Review - Consumer Reports"
        }
      ],
      "findings": "The base model of the Apple iPhone 16 starts at an official retail price of $799, while secondary market or reseller prices vary. Customer and expert reviews generally rate the iPhone 16 favorably as a strong, affordable entry into Apple's modern smartphone lineup, featuring improvements like the A18 chip and camera controls.\n\nLike all standard Apple hardware, the iPhone 16 comes with a standard one-year limited warranty provided by Apple, covering manufacturing defects in both parts and labor. Extended coverage can also be purchased separately through AppleCare+."
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "n:3",
    "kind": "upstream",
    "skill": "researcher",
    "output": {
      "question": "What is the price, customer rating, and warranty of Samsung Galaxy S25?",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://www.pcmag.com/reviews/samsung-galaxy-s25",
          "title": "Samsung Galaxy S25 Review - PCMag"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://www.gsmarena.com/samsung_galaxy_s25-review-2794.php",
          "title": "Samsung Galaxy S25 review - GSMArena.com tests"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://www.samsung.com/us/support/warranty/",
          "title": "Samsung Warranty: Check Your Samsung Products | Samsung US"
        }
      ],
      "findings": "The Samsung Galaxy S25 is positioned as a flagship smartphone starting at a base price around $799 / \u20ac799 / comparable regional pricing depending on storage configurations (such as 128GB or 256GB variants).\n\nCustomer ratings across major technology review outlets and retail platforms are generally positive, highlighting its compact form factor, upgraded performance via the Snapdragon 8 Elite chipset, and newly integrated Galaxy AI features, though some users note it represents an iterative update over previous generations.\n\nLike standard Samsung flagship mobile devices in major markets, the Galaxy S25 typically includes a 1-year manufacturer limited warranty covering defects in materials and workmanship, alongside standard regional consumer protection laws and optional extended coverage plans like Samsung Care+."
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "n:4",
    "kind": "upstream",
    "skill": "researcher",
    "output": {
      "question": "What is the price, customer rating, and warranty of Google Pixel 10?",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://mashable.com/review/google-pixel-10",
          "title": "Google Pixel 10 review: A fine Android phone with lots of... | Mashable"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://www.91mobiles.com/compare/Google/Pixel+10/vs/Samsung/Galaxy+S26+FE.html",
          "title": "Google Pixel 10 vs Samsung Galaxy S26 FE : Specs... | 91mobiles.com"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://hellosmartlife.com/how-long-is-google-pixel-warranty/",
          "title": "How Long is Google Pixel Warranty? (Uncovering the Truth)"
        }
      ],
      "findings": "The base model of the Google Pixel 10 starts at a price of $799, keeping the same launch price tier as its predecessor, the Pixel 9.\n\nCustomer and editorial reviews for the Google Pixel 10 are generally positive, receiving an expert rating of around 8.2 out of 10 from tech review aggregation (such as 91mobiles) and a solid 'Bang for the Buck' and performance score of 4 out of 5 in reviews like Mashable.\n\nLike standard Google Pixel hardware releases, the Google Pixel 10 comes with a standard one-year limited manufacturer warranty covering defects in parts and labor for the original purchaser, with optional extended protection plans like Pixel Care available for accidental damage."
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "n:5",
    "kind": "upstream",
    "skill": "coder",
    "output": {
      "code": "phones = [\n    {\"name\": \"iPhone 16\", \"price\": 799.0, \"rating\": 4.0, \"warranty\": 1},\n    {\"name\": \"Samsung Galaxy S25\", \"price\": 799.0, \"rating\": 4.0, \"warranty\": 1},\n    {\"name\": \"Google Pixel 10\", \"price\": 799.0, \"rating\": 4.0, \"warranty\": 1}\n]\n\nfor p in phones:\n    print(f\"{p['name']}: Price = ${p['price']:.2f}, Rating = {p['rating']}/5.0, Warranty = {p['warranty']} year\")\n\nprint(\"\\nComparison conclusion: All three phones share the exact same starting price ($799.00), standard manufacturer warranty (1 year), and generally positive reviews/ratings, making them tied in raw value based on available metrics.\")",
      "rationale": "Compare prices, ratings, and warranties of the three phones"
    }
  }
